verdicts.lean_check:
cd seedelf-verification && systemd-run --user --scope -q -p MemoryMax=8G -p MemorySwapMax=0 -p OOMPolicy=kill timeout 30m lake env lean /tmp/claude-1000/-home-logic-Documents-LogicalMechanism-Seedelf-Wallet/bb70aec6-fc56-4ac3-ac4c-9981682502da/scratchpad/check-flat-decoder/FlatDecodeCheck.lean

It imports Seedelf.Scripts, Lovejoin.Scripts, Lovejoin.Template.Scripts and Lovejoin.V2.Scripts (the built oleans) and refers to the scripts by their root-level names (wallet … mixLogicV2). It reads each script a second time, from Aiken's decode texts in …/check-flat-decoder/aiken/ (regenerate with `aiken uplc decode --hex --cbor <hex>`), through the conformance-tested textual parser.

Expected output:
- 16 "Successfully decoded textual" infos;
- `#eval` lines: 13 × `true`;
- then `false` three times (controls: wallet with q→q−1, always_false with one variable index changed, wallet vs seedelf);
- then `true` twice (v2 mix_logic = template applied to (B ab×28, B "lovejoin"); classic mix_box = template applied to (B 0dad3046…));
- no #guard error.

A `false` among the first 13 names a script whose ✅ is about a program other than its bytes, or a stale olean. A parse error is inconclusive. Do not run pcb-model/FlatVsText.lean as written: its fully qualified names (Seedelf.V1.wallet …) don't exist and it only prints unknown-identifier errors.
